msgstr "DESCRIPTION"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"These functions are obsolete: B<do not use them.> Use "
"B<pthread_attr_setstack>(3)  and B<pthread_attr_getstack>(3)  instead."
msgstr ""
"Ces fonctions sont obsolètes : B<ne les utilisez pas>. Utilisez "
"B<pthread_attr_setstack>(3) et B<pthread_attr_getstack>(3) à la place."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The B<pthread_attr_setstackaddr>()  function sets the stack address "
"attribute of the thread attributes object referred to by I<attr> to the "
"value specified in I<stackaddr>.  This attribute specifies the location of "
"the stack that should be used by a thread that is created using the thread "
"attributes object I<attr>."
msgstr ""
"La fonction B<pthread_attr_setstackaddr>() définit, à la valeur indiquée "
"dans I<adresse_pile>, l'attribut d'adresse de la pile de l'objet d'attributs "
"de thread I<attr>. Cet attribut indique l'emplacement de la pile qui devrait "
"être utilisée par un thread créé en utilisant l'objet d'attributs de thread "
"I<attr>."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"I<stackaddr> should point to a buffer of at least B<PTHREAD_STACK_MIN> bytes "
"that was allocated by the caller.  The pages of the allocated buffer should "
"be both readable and writable."
msgstr ""
"I<adresse_pile> devrait pointer vers un tampon d'au moins "
"B<PTHREAD_STACK_MIN> octets, alloué par l'appelant. Les pages du tampon "
"alloué devraient être accessibles à la fois en lecture et en écriture."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The B<pthread_attr_getstackaddr>()  function returns the stack address "
"attribute of the thread attributes object referred to by I<attr> in the "
"buffer pointed to by I<stackaddr>."
msgstr ""
"La fonction B<pthread_attr_getstackaddr>() renvoie, dans le tampon pointé "
"par I<adresse_pile>, l'attribut d'adresse de la pile de l'objet d'attributs "
"de thread I<attr>."

